            type: "Peach",
            name: "Eclipse",
            category: "Hardy peach varieties for Massachusetts from Fruit Notes 1953",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "22 days ahead of Elberta",
            description: "Fruit Notes describes Eclipse as a yellow-fleshed Elberta-type peach with medium to large freestone fruit, fair to good flavor, firm but sometimes coarse or stringy flesh, thin tender skin, high productivity, a need for severe thinning, and value where bud hardiness is the main concern"
        },
        {
